14
00:01:07.301 --> 00:01:14.280
Variables represent values and state,
expressions compute values, and control

15
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.770
structures select or repeat operations.

16
00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:25.232
Consider this worked case: A variable stores a
value that can change over time, while

17
00:01:25.232 --> 00:01:30.705
expressions compute new values based on
existing ones, and control structures

18
00:01:30.705 --> 00:01:33.192
determine which operations to execute.

19
00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:40.427
Trace each intermediate state in the example,
connect it to the formal claim, and verify

20
00:01:40.427 --> 00:01:44.286
that the final result satisfies the stated
condition.

21
00:01:44.286 --> 00:01:50.668
Separate the formal definition from an
implementation detail, then identify what

22
00:01:50.668 --> 00:01:52.989
