76
00:06:57.683 --> 00:07:04.990
Correctness arguments, tests, tracing, and
debugging compare intended behavior with

77
00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:10.105
observable results, including boundary and
error cases.

78
00:07:10.105 --> 00:07:17.852
Consider this worked case: Tests verify that
the program behaves as expected for various

79
00:07:17.852 --> 00:07:25.599
inputs, including edge cases, while tracing
follows the execution step by step to identify

80
00:07:25.599 --> 00:07:26.152
errors.

81
00:07:26.152 --> 00:07:33.357
Trace each intermediate state in the example,
connect it to the formal claim, and verify

82
00:07:33.357 --> 00:07:37.199
that the final result satisfies the stated
condition.

83
00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:44.881
Locate the first point where observed behavior
diverges from expected behavior, then test the

84
00:07:44.881 --> 00:07:46.527
